<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Abd al-Malik Imad al-Dawla</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1130</span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Abd al-Malik <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/imad-al-dawla">Imad al-Dawla</a> was the last Hudid ruler of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taifa">Taifa</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zaragoza">Zaragoza</a>. He succeeded his father <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ahmad-al-mustain-ii">al-Musta'in II</a> in 1110 but lost the city to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/almoravid-empire">Almoravids</a> that same year. Withdrawing to the strong castle of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rueda-de-jalon">Rueda de Jalón</a>, west of Zaragoza, he ruled a small territory from there with the support of the Christian kings of Aragon until his death in 1130.</p></div>
